      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ben Lomond was originally called Pacific Mills, named after a sawmill that operated there in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Lomond%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Between 1890 and 1940, Ben Lomond transformed from a logging outpost into a thriving tourist town with hotels and a library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://pressbanner.com/history-presentation-to-recount-ben-lomonds-early-years/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic Sanborn maps from 1908 reveal Ben Lomond’s early downtown layout, complete with labeled businesses, hotels, and schools.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hometownhistorymaps.com/pages/history-of-ben-lomond-california",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Ben Lomond Village Alliance, founded to preserve local heritage, organizes beautification projects and educational events for residents and visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://pressbanner.com/history-presentation-to-recount-ben-lomonds-early-years/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early 20th‑century Ben Lomond boasted a riverside park, a public hall, and a firehouse, marking its shift toward a self‑sufficient community.",
